WEBVTT

00:03.553 --> 00:05.521
And how are you this morning, Danny?

00:05.689 --> 00:08.089
Well, I didn't sleep very well...

00:08.258 --> 00:09.919
...last night, Alan.

00:10.393 --> 00:12.827
I had nightmares.

00:14.297 --> 00:16.527
Nightmares.

00:16.700 --> 00:19.294
Nightmares.

00:20.403 --> 00:24.499
I dreamed I ate a 5-pound marshmallow.

00:24.674 --> 00:26.642
A 5-pound marshmallow?

00:26.810 --> 00:31.440
Yeah. And when I woke up,
my pillow was gone.

00:33.550 --> 00:35.313
Pillow was gone.

00:35.485 --> 00:36.543
Pillow.

00:36.720 --> 00:40.178
Pillow. Pillow.

00:40.356 --> 00:42.620
- Alan?
- Yeah?

00:43.059 --> 00:45.550
You're starting to scare the crap
out of me.

00:46.029 --> 00:48.156
Oh, this? This is just a new hobby.

00:48.331 --> 00:51.129
Charlie, say hello to Danny O'Day.

00:51.301 --> 00:52.529
How do you do, Charlie?

00:53.703 --> 00:56.672
That's not a hobby, that's a cry for help.

00:57.373 --> 00:58.863
Oh, come on, Charlie, play along.

00:59.042 --> 01:01.738
So, Charlie, how did you sleep last night?

01:01.911 --> 01:03.503
With a woman, Alan.

01:07.283 --> 01:10.719
Something you need to do
before this gets out of hand.

01:11.921 --> 01:13.320
Oh.

01:13.690 --> 01:16.853
He's got a stick where I've got your hand.

01:18.394 --> 01:20.658
Did you ask him
if he wants to go to the movies?

01:20.830 --> 01:22.923
- No.
- Why not?

01:23.199 --> 01:24.826
Because he's a ticking time bomb...

01:25.001 --> 01:28.232
...and we don't wanna in the car with him
when he goes off.

01:29.172 --> 01:31.299
Come on, he's breaking my heart.

01:31.474 --> 01:33.772
Staying home all alone on a Friday night.

01:33.943 --> 01:35.035
Don't worry.

01:35.211 --> 01:37.771
You know how they say
you can be alone but not lonely?

01:38.047 --> 01:41.175
- Yeah.
- Well, Alan's kind of the opposite.

01:41.351 --> 01:44.445
He's always lonely, but he's never alone.

01:44.954 --> 01:46.444
He's going through a tough time.

01:46.656 --> 01:49.250
Your brother should be surrounded
by friends and family.

01:49.425 --> 01:51.950
My brother should be surrounded
by a SWAT team.

01:54.364 --> 01:56.457
Please? For me?

01:57.000 --> 02:00.060
Chelsea, we agreed
that you only get one of those a month.

02:00.236 --> 02:02.568
Are you sure
you wanna waste it on, Alan?

02:05.842 --> 02:08.276
Thanks for letting me tag along with you.

02:08.745 --> 02:10.542
This is really sweet.

02:10.713 --> 02:13.477
We're thrilled you could join us.
Right, Charlie?

02:14.317 --> 02:16.308
Yippee skippy.

02:16.886 --> 02:18.751
- So have we picked a movie yet?
- Nope.

02:18.922 --> 02:21.891
&lt;i>Would you like to see
La Poubelle et le Fromage at the Nuart?&lt;/i>

02:22.058 --> 02:23.719
Would I?

02:28.398 --> 02:32.994
Who you calling wood-eye, big ears?

02:34.137 --> 02:36.298
Now, Danny, watch your mouth.

02:36.739 --> 02:39.105
Why? Yours is the one that's moving.

02:44.781 --> 02:47.249
Yippee skippy.

03:22.051 --> 03:25.248
Hah. If she goes back to him
after what he's done...

03:25.421 --> 03:27.446
...I will never forgive her.

03:28.358 --> 03:31.191
She loves him.
What choice does she have?

03:31.361 --> 03:34.455
She can return to her husband,
the cheese maker.

03:39.002 --> 03:40.492
Listen, I'm gonna hit the head.

03:40.670 --> 03:43.662
Let me know
if any kind of a plot ever kicks in.

03:48.344 --> 03:50.209
He's not coming back is he?

03:50.380 --> 03:51.677
They sell beer in the lobby?

03:51.848 --> 03:53.475
- Yes.
- No.

04:13.403 --> 04:16.270
You're up early for a Saturday morning.

04:16.439 --> 04:19.670
Hence, the cock-a-doodle-doo.

04:23.012 --> 04:25.412
Chelsea? It's 7:30.
We gotta get a move on.

04:25.581 --> 04:29.813
Oh, God, that's right. I forgot.
Give me a few minutes to get dressed.

04:29.986 --> 04:32.045
No problem. I'll wait for you downstairs.

04:32.221 --> 04:35.156
- What's going on?
- Your brother and I are going to the market.

04:42.298 --> 04:43.890
Since when?

04:44.067 --> 04:45.796
We made plans last night.

04:45.969 --> 04:47.334
Last night when?

04:47.503 --> 04:50.472
In the movie theater,
while you were in the lobby drinking.

04:50.907 --> 04:55.037
Well, I wasn't gonna go sit in the car
with that scary dummy.

04:56.079 --> 04:58.912
I like mustard...

04:59.082 --> 05:01.277
...and pickles...

05:01.451 --> 05:05.649
...and ketchup and mayonnaise.

05:07.023 --> 05:08.354
Mayonnaise.

05:09.425 --> 05:11.586
Mayonnaise.

05:11.761 --> 05:13.092
You and me need to talk.

05:14.130 --> 05:16.121
How do you do, Charlie?

05:16.866 --> 05:18.766
Get that ugly thing out of my face.

05:19.502 --> 05:21.902
That's what she said.

05:26.709 --> 05:29.576
Oh, Danny. Danny, you're horrible. Heh.

05:30.380 --> 05:31.870
My hand to God, Alan...

05:32.048 --> 05:35.313
...I will wrap that dummy with meat
and throw him in the ocean.

05:36.085 --> 05:39.486
Don't forget the mayonnaise.

05:43.126 --> 05:44.684
Ow.

05:46.295 --> 05:48.058
I'm okay.

05:49.932 --> 05:52.662
Why are you taking Chelsea
to that farmer's thing?

05:52.969 --> 05:56.370
- Is there a problem?
- Yeah. You're ruining my Saturday.

05:56.539 --> 05:59.736
- I'm sorry, did you have plans for the day?
- Damn right, I had plans.

05:59.909 --> 06:03.310
First, I was gonna have sex with Chelsea.
And then...

06:03.479 --> 06:05.845
Well, then I was gonna go back to sleep.

06:06.716 --> 06:08.206
You can still go back to sleep.

06:08.384 --> 06:10.648
Yeah, but without sex,
it's a restless sleep.

06:11.654 --> 06:14.054
- Fine, fine. I'll just go by myself.
- No, no.

06:14.223 --> 06:16.691
If you go without her now,
then I'm the bad guy.

06:16.859 --> 06:18.292
So, what do you want me to do?

06:18.461 --> 06:21.692
In the future, I want you
to be more sensitive and considerate...

06:21.864 --> 06:23.229
...to other peoples needs.

06:23.566 --> 06:24.658
Okay.

06:24.834 --> 06:26.165
Thank you.

06:26.335 --> 06:29.099
If you'll excuse me,
I'm gonna join Chelsea in the shower...

06:29.272 --> 06:31.399
...and try to knock out a quick one.

06:33.643 --> 06:35.702
Oh, Danny.

06:36.846 --> 06:40.680
Sometimes he can be such a pig.

06:41.250 --> 06:43.844
Well, you know what happens to pigs.

06:45.254 --> 06:46.744
They get slaught-

06:47.423 --> 06:50.392
Danny, don't say it. Don't even think it.

06:52.361 --> 06:54.352
- Ered.

07:21.757 --> 07:23.088
What are you looking at?

07:23.259 --> 07:25.056
JAKE: Nothing.

07:31.701 --> 07:33.430
Hey, hey.

07:33.603 --> 07:37.004
What are you doing here?
Thought you were with your mom and Herb.

07:37.173 --> 07:38.333
I was supposed to...

07:38.508 --> 07:40.408
...but Mom's got those
pregnancy hormones going.

07:41.177 --> 07:42.542
What did you do?

07:42.712 --> 07:45.272
One little fat joke.

07:46.015 --> 07:47.141
Took it badly, eh?

07:47.316 --> 07:48.977
Well, here I am.

07:50.620 --> 07:51.848
Where's Dad?

07:52.021 --> 07:53.648
He went out with Chelsea.

07:53.823 --> 07:57.088
- You mean like a date?
- No. No, not a date.

07:57.260 --> 07:59.592
Good, because that'd be weird.

08:00.463 --> 08:01.487
Yeah.

08:01.664 --> 08:04.599
&lt;i>I saw something like that
on Jerry Springer once.&lt;/i>

08:05.902 --> 08:08.132
Two brothers, one girl. It got ugly.

08:09.505 --> 08:10.802
I'm sure it did.

08:12.942 --> 08:14.603
So, what's Dad's dummy doing here?

08:15.211 --> 08:17.179
It pissed off his mother.

08:21.784 --> 08:23.149
Oh.

08:23.553 --> 08:25.316
Hey, I did that too.

08:32.728 --> 08:35.561
Okay. Please take this kettle corn away
from me.

08:35.731 --> 08:38.131
I can feel it going right to my behind.

08:40.169 --> 08:41.261
Oh, stop it.

08:41.437 --> 08:43.371
I wish my tush was as small as yours.

08:43.539 --> 08:46.201
Okay, first of all,
you have a perfect heinie.

08:46.375 --> 08:50.243
Secondly, if you're worried about firmness,
the secret is isometric glute crunches.

08:50.479 --> 08:52.538
- Really?
- You can do them anywhere, any time.

08:52.715 --> 08:54.740
I'm doing them right now. See?

08:55.251 --> 08:58.448
Mailbox open, mailbox closed.

08:58.721 --> 09:00.655
Mailbox open, mailbox closed.

09:01.757 --> 09:03.850
Come on, try it with me.

09:04.493 --> 09:07.291
- Mailbox open, mailbox closed.
- Mailbox open, mailbox closed.

09:07.463 --> 09:10.489
- Mailbox open, mailbox closed.
- Mailbox open, mailbox closed.

09:10.666 --> 09:12.827
Mailbox open, mailbox-

09:14.570 --> 09:19.007
You know, just once I'd like to walk
in this room and not be freaked out.

09:21.077 --> 09:23.739
Alan was just showing me
his butt exercises.

09:24.013 --> 09:27.540
Have him show you the one where he sticks
his head up there. My favorite.

09:28.150 --> 09:30.550
Stop it.
Now, go away, were making dinner.

09:33.022 --> 09:35.616
- It's kind of like a Kegel exercise, isn't it?
- Uh- Exactly.

09:35.791 --> 09:38.123
Except with tush not the hoo-ha.

09:50.539 --> 09:52.302
What up, homes?

09:53.843 --> 09:55.174
What are you doing?

09:55.344 --> 09:57.539
Enjoying the sunset, waiting on dinner.

09:57.980 --> 09:59.641
You're staying for dinner?

09:59.815 --> 10:04.650
I wasn't gonna, but your lovely fiancée
and her new gal pal insisted.

10:06.289 --> 10:09.816
Yeah, I gotta put a stop to that.

10:10.126 --> 10:11.525
What, are you nuts?

10:11.694 --> 10:13.491
This is a perfect setup for you.

10:14.063 --> 10:16.588
- How do you figure?
- Do you like to go shopping?

10:17.033 --> 10:19.558
- No.
- Zippy does.

10:19.902 --> 10:21.494
Do you like to watch chick flicks?

10:21.971 --> 10:24.439
- No.
- Zippy does.

10:24.607 --> 10:26.939
Do you like to talk for hours
about your feelings?

10:27.276 --> 10:29.767
- No.
- Zippy do.

10:30.813 --> 10:32.940
Oh, right.

10:33.115 --> 10:35.811
He digs the trench, you lay the pipe.

10:37.286 --> 10:39.049
How could I not see this?

10:39.221 --> 10:42.452
Alan's not the competition,
he's her gay friend.

10:42.625 --> 10:44.525
There you go. Your life is perfect.

10:45.294 --> 10:46.989
- It is, isn't it?
- Yeah.

10:47.163 --> 10:50.826
- Now, be an angel and get me another beer.
- Absolutely.

10:54.904 --> 10:57.134
Jiminy, I'm drunk.

11:03.379 --> 11:05.210
Oh, I hate to do this to you.

11:05.481 --> 11:07.847
But using the existing S
in the top row...

11:08.017 --> 11:14.445
...with R-E before it,
and I-Z-I-N-G after it...

11:14.623 --> 11:20.391
...hitting two triple-word scores
and it's a bingo.

11:20.563 --> 11:23.191
"Resizing," 120 points.

11:23.566 --> 11:26.126
Oh, my God,
you play for blood, don't you?

11:26.302 --> 11:27.496
Let me tell you something.

11:27.670 --> 11:31.470
When it comes to Scrabble,
nice guys finish with a rack full of tiles.

11:37.246 --> 11:38.873
What do you mean it's not a word?

11:39.048 --> 11:40.879
It's not a word. Try again.

11:41.050 --> 11:42.449
CHARLIE:
Hmm.

11:42.618 --> 11:43.676
Charlie, horny.

11:45.821 --> 11:47.982
- Another glass of wine?
- I would love one.

11:54.597 --> 11:57.225
Now?
But Alan and I are playing Scrabble.

11:57.633 --> 12:00.693
Well, I'm playing Scrabble.
I don't know what she's doing.

12:02.772 --> 12:05.605
I'm improving is what I'm doing.
I want a rematch.

12:08.210 --> 12:09.939
Good night, Alan.

12:11.213 --> 12:12.544
But I just poured wine.

12:12.948 --> 12:14.006
Oh, thanks.

12:15.384 --> 12:17.716
And thanks for being such a good friend
to Chelsea.

12:17.987 --> 12:20.046
I like her and we've got a lot in common.

12:20.222 --> 12:23.487
Yeah, whatever. Just keep it up.
And I'll try to do the same.

12:28.464 --> 12:31.627
Kind of ruin the night.

12:36.439 --> 12:38.100
He's using you.

12:39.742 --> 12:42.108
I know. What am I gonna do?

12:42.845 --> 12:46.110
You could kill him.

12:48.517 --> 12:50.712
Now, Danny, I could never do that.

12:51.187 --> 12:53.018
Don't worry, Alan.

12:53.189 --> 12:56.249
I can do it for you.

13:07.203 --> 13:08.636
- Morning.
Morning.

13:08.804 --> 13:11.932
- Hope you're hungry, I made pancakes.
- Oh, I'm starving. Can I help?

13:12.107 --> 13:14.575
Sure. Slice up some bananas
and warm up the syrup.

13:14.743 --> 13:16.768
- I'm on it.
- Sleep well?

13:17.580 --> 13:20.572
Yeah. I mean, when your brother
finally let me go to sleep.

13:24.487 --> 13:26.352
- Can I tell you a little secret?
- Sure.

13:27.256 --> 13:31.750
- He's the best lover I've ever had.
- Oh, isn't that nice.

13:31.927 --> 13:34.828
Yeah, it's great. But sometimes
he doesn't know when to quit.

13:35.397 --> 13:37.524
Have you tried pepper spray?

13:37.800 --> 13:41.531
No. But every once in a while,
I actually have to give him a little smack...

13:41.704 --> 13:43.171
...on the top of his head.

13:43.339 --> 13:46.536
Yeah, I have the same problem
with Jake when he eats spaghetti.

13:46.876 --> 13:50.812
Well, obviously, not the same problem.
Jake's head is usually over here.

13:52.114 --> 13:55.311
Don't get me wrong, I'm not complaining,
but it can be exhausting.

13:55.484 --> 13:58.476
I can imagine.
Have you given Charlie enough attaboys?

13:58.921 --> 14:01.389
- Attaboys?
- You know, like when you're training a dog.

14:01.557 --> 14:05.687
If you don't give them hugs and a treat,
they're gonna chew up your rug.

14:05.861 --> 14:07.988
I mean, not your rug.

14:08.797 --> 14:10.492
Hey, how are those bananas coming?

14:11.967 --> 14:14.800
- Morning.
- Morning. How'd you sleep?

14:14.970 --> 14:16.301
Good.

14:16.472 --> 14:17.564
When you finally let me.

14:17.740 --> 14:19.503
Hush.

14:20.476 --> 14:21.534
Alan's making pancakes.

14:21.710 --> 14:24.873
- Can I pour you some coffee?
- I would love that.

14:25.447 --> 14:27.574
Good morning, Mrs. Butterworth.

14:30.953 --> 14:33.319
Oh. Lakers-Spurs today.

14:33.489 --> 14:35.548
You promised we'd go
to the van Gogh exhibit.

14:35.824 --> 14:37.815
- I did?
- Yes.

14:38.127 --> 14:39.719
Wow, I don't remember that.

14:39.895 --> 14:42.159
You gotta quit hitting me
on the head so much.

14:42.998 --> 14:46.661
I've heard that exhibit is supposed
to be terrific. I've been dying to see it.

14:47.069 --> 14:49.435
Really? Then why don't we all go.

14:49.605 --> 14:51.732
I can't.
I promised Jake we'd do something.

14:52.041 --> 14:53.099
Bring him along.

14:53.275 --> 14:56.676
What 14-year-old boy
doesn't love a fine-art museum?

14:57.413 --> 14:59.779
That's a great idea,
you and Jake come with us.

14:59.949 --> 15:02.850
- Well, if you don't think we'd be intruding.
- No, not at all.

15:03.018 --> 15:04.781
Okay, great. Heh-heh-heh.

15:05.054 --> 15:06.180
Save me some pancakes.

15:06.355 --> 15:08.016
I'm gonna shower and get ready.

15:08.190 --> 15:11.387
Hurry. I wanna get to the museum
before it's too crowded.

15:11.560 --> 15:13.289
Now, here's the deal.

15:14.663 --> 15:16.528
You're gonna go to the museum
without me.

15:16.699 --> 15:19.827
- Why?
- I am about to get an acute case...

15:20.002 --> 15:21.230
...of intestinal distress.

15:21.403 --> 15:24.600
- What?
- You know, the flapjack two-step.

15:25.507 --> 15:29.500
- There's nothing wrong with my pancakes.
- No, they're delightful.

15:29.678 --> 15:32.238
But Lakers are playing the Spurs,
I'm not gonna miss it.

15:32.414 --> 15:35.212
So what, so you're gonna use me
to entertain your fiancée...

15:35.384 --> 15:37.716
...while you stay home
and watch a basketball game?

15:37.886 --> 15:39.353
Good, we're on the same page.

15:39.521 --> 15:42.217
Did you ever stop to think
maybe I've got plans of my own?

15:42.391 --> 15:45.326
That I've got a life,
that I'm not always at your beck and call.

15:46.795 --> 15:48.456
No.

15:57.640 --> 16:01.872
You know, Berta, I thought when Alan
moved in here, I was being punished.

16:02.044 --> 16:04.137
You and me both.

16:05.381 --> 16:08.407
But come to find out, it was a blessing.

16:08.584 --> 16:12.486
With him in my life, I think I can actually
make my relationship with Chelsea work.

16:13.355 --> 16:15.448
So you're gonna go through
with this marriage?

16:15.624 --> 16:18.149
Absolutely.
I'm ready for the whole shebang.

16:18.327 --> 16:19.794
Kids too?

16:20.396 --> 16:22.626
Well, it's certainly in the cards.

16:22.798 --> 16:26.097
Of course, I'd have to talk it over
with Chelsea and Alan first.

16:28.504 --> 16:31.769
Wow, marriage and kids.
I can't believe what I'm hearing.

16:32.641 --> 16:34.233
What can I say, Berta?

16:34.410 --> 16:36.310
He completes me.

16:45.254 --> 16:46.915
One second.

16:48.190 --> 16:51.318
- Ha. He's hilarious.
- Who?

16:51.627 --> 16:54.118
Your brother. I-O-I.

16:55.597 --> 16:57.155
All right.

17:02.304 --> 17:05.034
Let me just tell him we'll talk tomorrow.

17:06.842 --> 17:08.810
He is out of control.

17:08.977 --> 17:11.207
- What now?
- Hang on.

17:13.248 --> 17:16.411
"Don't let him chew up the rug."

17:18.053 --> 17:19.918
- What does that mean?
- Nothing.

17:20.723 --> 17:23.055
Why would I chew up a rug?

17:23.659 --> 17:26.651
Not a rug, my- Never mind.

17:29.698 --> 17:31.598
Okay, where were we?

17:32.000 --> 17:34.127
We just about-

17:36.538 --> 17:38.438
I'm sure he just wants to say good night.

17:49.384 --> 17:51.978
I'm sorry.
Let me just make sure he's okay.

17:54.990 --> 17:56.924
Is he okay?

17:58.927 --> 18:01.794
- Yeah.
- Good, good.

18:01.964 --> 18:04.728
- Hey, I'm thirsty. Are you thirsty?
- No.

18:04.900 --> 18:06.868
- Be right back.
- Hurry.

18:07.035 --> 18:10.334
Don't worry.
This won't take but a minute.

18:15.110 --> 18:19.809
Oh, Charlie, your penis
is no match for my technology.

18:21.683 --> 18:24.243
Okay, I know what you're doing,
now quit it.

18:24.620 --> 18:26.485
What I'm doing? Whatever do you mean?

18:26.655 --> 18:28.555
You're text-blocking me.

18:29.658 --> 18:32.718
Hey, I can't help it
if Chelsea finds me witty and urbane.

18:32.895 --> 18:36.387
Keep it up and she's gonna find you
bloody and homeless.

18:37.733 --> 18:39.223
You don't scare me, Charlie.

18:39.401 --> 18:41.460
You need me
to keep Chelsea off your back.

18:42.137 --> 18:46.039
That may be true, but I don't need him.

18:46.208 --> 18:48.506
Wait, wait. Just let him go, Charlie.

18:49.077 --> 18:51.602
- This is just between you and me.
- Not anymore.

18:51.780 --> 18:53.111
Don't you dare hurt him.

18:53.549 --> 18:56.882
Well, now, that's entirely up to you.

18:57.052 --> 18:59.850
His tiny, wooden head is in your hands.

19:03.492 --> 19:05.119
Charlie?

19:05.427 --> 19:06.451
Danny!

19:09.998 --> 19:12.466
Just let him go now.
- Charlie?

19:15.003 --> 19:17.198
What the hell are you doing?

19:18.674 --> 19:21.472
- Nothing.
- Nothing.

19:21.643 --> 19:23.338
Nothing.

19:29.084 --> 19:30.847
You should be ashamed of yourself.

19:31.019 --> 19:32.748
That's no way for a grown man to behave.

19:32.921 --> 19:34.047
CHARLIE:
He started it.

19:34.223 --> 19:35.884
I don't care who started it.

19:36.058 --> 19:38.583
You're the older brother,
you set the example.

19:38.760 --> 19:41.228
